{"title":"1981 IMO Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/f/f6fa69bf141527c27a71998fbb0bfd4a8493fce6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"18\" /> satisfies\n</p><p>(1) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/f/dcf9a36edfd5b482a9f8de51afddcbd2755376b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(0,y)=y+1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"121\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>(2) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/6/4c6201512df69c6ed49b1433819f0e7de8d8630e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x+1,0)=f(x,1),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"164\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>(3) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/b/e5bd371ca3104247dbf757b602acac5b4bf090da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x+1,y+1)=f(x,f(x+1,y)),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"271\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>for all non-negative integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/4/b6400c6fe3f1ed70e5afd387a9686cdc3fa09531.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"11\" />. Determine <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/b/6db1a1d1a8d9dd85048547167a61c78aff215e0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(4,1981)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We observe that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/7/767968c8b01d9c11d6858d0b6f6b3608c5af8b83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1,0) = f(0,1) = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"159\" height=\"18\" /> and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/7/f47d70ee1c82fa96687d0269b205cda18fdd3866.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1, y+1) = f(0, f(1,y)) = f(1,y) + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"310\" height=\"20\" />, so by induction, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/acc7b6a05fef1c3d37a3c78f4989189fa33ad61a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1,y) = y+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"119\" height=\"20\" />.  Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/9/149cea90a98b4165acf02f9bc1574c39f8b70ab8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2,0) = f(1,1) = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"159\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/3/2b3ff845457a70408b6f607624fc21a42e86fc0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2, y+1) = f(2,y) + 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"189\" height=\"18\" />, yielding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/5/705bcbe927a0f87323946ab53ac7f81651a31a2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2,y) = 2y + 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"125\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>We continue with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/b/64b881b4fe3729ef1b72d1d5200c33d92345f50b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(3,0) + 3 = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"18\" />; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/0/50040130d7a914bbf751c8f14fb6925e21a8fc95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(3, y+1) + 3 = 2(f(3,y) + 3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"243\" height=\"18\" />; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/f/caf00b46bd91467e2c19c037685821a0b62309d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(3,y) + 3 = 2^{y+3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"139\" height=\"19\" />; and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/4/3b41b3462be6526b402ea378d283cd42e11fc2ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(4,0) + 3 = 2^{2^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"127\" height=\"23\" />; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/5/9c5b468bb40be9b7951be01859acec27e54a9348.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(4,y) + 3 = 2^{f(4,y-1) + 3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"189\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/d/56d5c15729f4bde20f9f45c22a7d0b0f0f310fe1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(4,1981) = 2^{2\\cdot ^{ . \\cdot 2}} - 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"168\" height=\"23\" /> when there are 1984 2s, Q.E.D.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can start by creating a list consisting of certain x an y values and their outputs. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/e/92ee4f88458bfa8e3d7236c5b9f666bc9fb50b21.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(0,0)=1,   f(0,1)=2,  f(0,2)=3, f(0,3)=4, f(0,4)=5\\]\" width=\"454\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>This pattern can be proved using induction. After proving, we continue to setting a list when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/2/69271b422e022ea65ff1f288eddfcfa82afd8ab7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/65130767fa649bd07215e0316ab1986aa6544e31.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(1,0)=2,   f(1,1)=3,  f(1,2)=4, f(1,3)=5, f(1,4)=6\\]\" width=\"454\" height=\"18\" /> This pattern can also be proved using induction. The pattern seems d up of a common difference of 1. Moving on to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/2/b022dc8ef6d33931fc1ae3d27df3ea0a81b52936.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/9/399bfbd77170f86c9a3d8b68ca3d2a74c05e49cb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(3,0)=5,   f(3,1)=13,  f(3,2)=29, f(3,3)=61, f(3,4)=125\\]\" width=\"499\" height=\"18\" /> All of the numbers are being expressed in the form of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/5/9756dc4ba03d6f1a9ac46d09126717bd74993bb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^a -3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"16\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/e/69ef6c6221363b04590d3f955315f99745592f64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=y+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"17\" />. Lastly where x=4 we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/e/bbec9e553d2fe1cf95fbb734b446dcb275d0f2d1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(4,0)=13,   f(4,1)=65533,  f(4,2)=^5 2-3, f(4,3)=^6 2-3, f(4,4)=^7 2-3\\]\" width=\"591\" height=\"20\" /> where each term can be represented as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/8/ef802e5fe1ff39943db04fc9a3e13c08cfda8d61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$^a 2-3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"16\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/3/2e389caa8c956a8dd8cec99728cc4906596da880.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=y+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"17\" />. In <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/8/d089fd079b371593c7a9f6b86f3ff64af8d5f825.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$^a 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> represents tetration or 2 to the power 2 to the power 2 to the power 2 ... where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> amount of 2s. So therefore the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/d/56d5c15729f4bde20f9f45c22a7d0b0f0f310fe1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(4,1981) = 2^{2\\cdot ^{ . \\cdot 2}} - 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"168\" height=\"23\" /> with 1984 2s, 2  tetration 1983.\n-Multpi12\n</p><p><br />\n<b>Remark.</b> This function is well-studied, known widely as the Ackermann function.\n</p><p><i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1981_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_IMO\" title=\"1981 IMO\">1981 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1981 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1981 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1981 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1981 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1981 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1981 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1981 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last question</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017173647\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.026 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.044 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 166/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1210/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 51/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5858/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   11.975      1 -total\n 53.59%    6.417      1 Template:IMO_box\n 45.39%    5.435      1 Template:Alternate_solutions\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:4018:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017173647 and revision id 287294. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}